{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JHN",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Jesus",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " passed by, he saw a man who was blind from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " birth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his disciples asked him, saying, Master, who sinned, this man, or his parents, that he was born blind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered, Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh when no man can work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As long as I am in the world, I am the light of the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he had thus spoken, he spit on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and he anointed the eyes of the blind man with the clay,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam, (which is by interpretation, Sent.) He went therefore, and washed, and came seeing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The neighbors therefore, and they who before had seen him that he was blind, said, Is not this he that sat and begged?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Some said, This is he: others ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "said",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", He is like him: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he said, I am ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore they said to him, How were thy eyes opened?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He answered and said, A man that is called Jesus, made clay, and anointed my eyes, and said to me, Go to the pool of Siloam, and wash: and I went and washed, and I received sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said they to him, Where is he? He said, I know not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They brought to the Pharisees him that before was blind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was the sabbath when Jesus made the clay, and opened his eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then again the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight. He said to them, He put clay upon my eyes, and I washed, and do see.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore said some of the Pharisees, This man is not from God, because he keepeth not the sabbath. Others said, How can a man that is a sinner do such miracles? And there was a division among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They say to the blind man again, What sayest thou of him, that he hath opened thy eyes? He said, He is a prophet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the Jews did not believe concerning him that he had been blind, and received his sight, until they called the parents of him that had received his sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they asked them, saying, Is this your son, who ye say was born blind? how then doth he now see?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His parents answered them and said, We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But by what means he now seeth, we know not; or who hath opened his eyes, we know not: he is of age; ask him: he will speak for himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "words",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his parents spoke, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had agreed already, that if any man confessed that he was Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore said his parents, He is of age; ask him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then again they called the man that was blind, and said to him, Give God the praise: we know that this man is a sinner.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He answered and said, Whether he is a sinner, I know not: one thing I know, that whereas I was blind, now I see.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they said to him again, What did he to thee? how opened he thy eyes?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He answered them, I have told you already, and ye did not hear: Why would ye hear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " again? will ye also be his disciples?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they reviled him, and said, Thou art his disciple; but we are the disciples of Moses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We know that God spoke to Moses: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", we know not whence he is.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The man answered and said to them, Why, herein is a marvelous thing, that ye know not from whence he is, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath opened my eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now we know that God heareth not sinners: but if any man is a worshiper of God, and doeth his will, him he heareth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Since the world began hath it not been heard that any man opened the eyes of one that was born blind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If this man were not from God, he could do nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They answered and said to him, Thou wast altogether born in sins, and dost thou teach us? and they cast him out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus heard that they had cast him out: and when he had found him, he said to him, Dost thou believe on the Son of God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He answered and said, Who is he, Lord, that I may believe on him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus said to him, thou hast both seen him, and it is he that talketh with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Lord, I believe. And he worshiped him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus said, For judgment I am come into this world, that they who see not, may see; and that they who see, may be made blind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the Pharisees who were with him heard these words, and said to him, Are we blind also?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.9.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.9.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus said to them, If ye were blind, ye would have no sin: but now ye say, We see; therefore your sin remaineth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
